.TH fractal 1A
.SH NAME
fractal, julia \- Display Mandelbrot and Julia sets on Amiga Unix
/dev/screen device
.SH SYNOPSIS
fractal
[-?JMbB] [-xyiIpPqaeHWDhwdmf float]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fractal
commands have changed from the previous release.  New mouse and
key hacks are available.
.B fractal
by default opens the largest possible screen on the default monitor
under the screens device (/dev/screen).
.B fractal proceeds to display a Mandelbrot (or Julia) set
for the current coordinates.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
J
Julia computation.
.TP
M
Mandelbrot computation
.TP
x float
X (real component of Z) center of fractal to compute.
.TP
y float
Y (imaginary component of Z) center of fractal to compute.
.TP
i float
X interation increment.
.TP
I float
Y interation increment.
.TP
p float
real componant of C.
.TP
q imaginary component of C.
.TP
a
Attractor point.  Interration of Z = Z^2 + C will stop when
Z is greater than a.
.TP
e
Escape point or max interrations.  Interration of Z = Z^2 + C will
terminate if the interration number exceeds e.
.TP
w
Actual screen width.
.TP
h
Actual screen height.
.TP
d
Actual screen depth.
.TP
f
scrtype flags (see screen(1A)).
.TP
m
scrtype modes (see screen(1A)).
.TP
W
Virtual screen width.
.TP
H
Virtual screen height.
.TP
D
Virtual screen depth.
.TP
B
Batch mode (no display, save on exit)
.TP
b
Same as `B' (batch mode) but will display screen while fractal is
being computed.
.TP
F
Filename for Amiga-s (save gif file) key hack.
.SH MOUSE HACKS
To zoom into the fractal drag a box around the part of the fractal
you wish to display.  If the SHIFT key is held down while dragging the
mouse the box will not be contrained to square sides.

If a zoom box is displayed and CONTROL key is held down while dragging
the mouse the zoom box will move.  If no zoom box is display the screen
will move around the virtual screen (see command line options -H, -W,
and -D).

Use Amiga-z (or the RETURN key) to zoom in, Amiga-Z to zoom out.

Use ESC to terminate zoom box mode.
.SH KEY HACKS
Most key hacks are now modified by the Amiga-key.
.TP
Amiga-q
Quit fractal.
.TP
ESC
Quit a zoom grab.
.TP
Amiga-c
Change the color map.  See the section
.B COLORS
for more information.
.TP
TAB
Toggle color cycling.
.TP
Amiga-s
Save fractal as frac.gif in current directory.
.TP
Amiga-j
Redraw the Julia Set that corresonds to the position of the pointer.
(only valid while drawing a Mandlebrot Set).
.TP
Amiga-m
Redraw the Mandelbrot Set that corresonds to the position of the pointer.
(only valid while drawing a Julia Set).
.TP
Amiga-w
Write out a gif file of the current screen using the current name
given on the command line with the -F argument.
.SH COLOR
While in color mode you can use the pointer to click on one of the
color boxs representing your current color palette and change it by selecting the
color in the color selection box to the left or by dragging the red, green, and
blue slide gadgets at the bottom of the screen that correspond to 
red, green, and blue color intensities.  Use the Return Key to return
the fractal with the new colors installed.  Use ESC to abort.
.SH NOTES
This version of
.B Fractal 
has a better user interface then the previous version but it still
need work.  If you'd like to work on it--do it.  Please
send me any hacks you have for it.
.PP
Partial hacks are in for raising Z to an arbitrary power.  I did not
have time to finish this so the code lay in NEWcompute.c in the source
directory.  It is slow as a dog.
.PP
There needs to be a text interface to dump and modify the current fractal
coordinates.  This was deemed to hairy for 2.0.
.PP
I ment to fix up a 4-d fractal render program.  There is a simple
attempt called fracslice and is in the source directory.  Maybe
someone can use it.
.PP
scrcols (the color selection) is actually a separate program. You
may use it to set your text screen, cursor colors.  scrcols has problems
on systems that by default use overscan.
.PP
Someday I will write a decent manual page.
